<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shah Jahan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1592">1592</a>–<a href="/years/1666">1666</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shah Jahan was the fifth Mughal emperor, ruling from 1628 to 1658. His reign marked the height of Mughal architecture, with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taj-mahal">Taj Mahal</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/agra">Agra</a>, built for his wife Mumtaz Mahal, and the new capital of Shahjahanabad at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi">Delhi</a>. He annexed the Ahmadnagar Sultanate in 1636 and granted lands to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajputs">Rajput</a> lords such as those of Kota, Shahpura and Ratlam. His son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aurangzeb">Aurangzeb</a> deposed him in 1658 and kept him confined at Agra until his death.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/shah-jahan.jpg" alt="Shah Jahan" width="320" height="463" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bichitr · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%27Jujhar_Singh_Bundela_Kneels_in_Submission_to_Shah_Jahan%27,_painted_by_Bichitr,_c._1630,_Chester_Beatty_Library_(cropped2).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
